> at you, then how mean the monster was stops mattering.  Once
> you start seeing clovers a newt is as good as a dragon.  Same
> change of an artifact or clover.

This is not true. Monsters don't have a chance of mollifying the god; 
certain monsters have very specific values, and your god has a specific 
amount of anger towards you. Some monsters are worth more mollifying 
points than others, but there's no randomness involved; either a type of 
creature will reduce anger or it won't. Chaotic gods are harder to 
mollify than Lawful or Neutral ones. See

http://www.nethack.de/spoiler/appeasement.txt

for a list of creature values. Basically, you can sacrifice all the 
newts in the world and you'll never appease your god.

Also, after you've gotten rid of the prayer timeout, the power of the 
monster does still matter; not all clovers are equal. A clover 
represents a gain of 1 to 5 luck depending on the level of the creature.


